# basedverse's settings: a template, with nothing real in it. Copy what you need into a .env (never
# committed; .gitignore keeps it out) and fill it in. Blank means the default. `bin/setup` writes the first
# section into a workroom's .env for you, asking for what it needs.

# -- A workroom's visit-client (visit/INTEGRATING.md, step 2) ---------------------------------------------
# visit-client reads these from its environment (each is also a flag: VISIT_PORT is --port). A workroom
# keeps them in its own settings, its .env say, starting from this section, and its launcher passes them on.

# The lobby's address, from whoever runs it: wss://<its IP address or DNS name>/
VISIT_LOBBY=
# The office's name in the lobby: 1-24 letters, digits, space, _ . -, starting and ending with a letter or
# digit. In quotes if it has a space ("My Room"), so a shell can load this file too.
VISIT_NAME=
# The sim, as name/version, shown to others, e.g. my-workroom/1.0 (default unknown/0).
VISIT_SIM=
# visit-client's port on 127.0.0.1, for the workroom's page (default 7401).
VISIT_PORT=
# How many visitors the room takes at once, 0-8 (default 3).
VISIT_MAX_VISITORS=
# The page's origins, comma-separated: scheme://host:port as the address bar shows them, e.g.
# http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000. visit-client refuses any other site's page, token or not.
# Blank lets any page with the token in: name yours.
VISIT_ORIGINS=
# The file the launcher writes a new page token to on every run (mode 0600). The token itself never goes
# in a .env: it is new each run.
VISIT_TOKEN_FILE=
# The relays for links, overriding the lobby's: none, default (iroh's public ones), or comma-separated
# URLs (default: the ones the lobby names).
VISIT_RELAYS=
# A file where visit-client keeps what outlasts a run: whether the office went offline (the panel's Go
# offline, or leaveLobby()), so a restart stays offline; the office's key, so it is the same office to the
# friends who made it their guest; its door and its guests. A secret (it holds the key: visit-client makes
# it readable by you only): the user's own, outside any repository, written out in full (no ~), e.g.
# /home/you/.local/state/basedverse/my-room.json (bin/setup picks one). Blank: every start joins the lobby,
# with a new key and no guests.
VISIT_STATE_FILE=
# Where visit-client keeps friends' landscapes (the parts of their rooms that never change: sent once) and their
# plots to draw while they are away. Blank: landscapes/ beside VISIT_STATE_FILE (or, without one, for the run only).
VISIT_CACHE_DIR=
# visit-client's database (required, Visit 0.20): Postgres beside it, where it keeps the chat its user has had, the
# pictures and links shared in it, and whom its room keeps out. postgres://user:password@host:port/database. A
# secret (it holds the password). bin/setup can start one in Docker and write it here. Made ready, and brought up to
# date after every upgrade, by: visit-client migrate (it reads this).
VISIT_DATABASE_URL=
# Exit after this many seconds with no page connected (default 0: never).
VISIT_IDLE_EXIT=
# Not visit-client's but its launcher's: where visit-client is (bin/setup puts it in
# visit/client/bin/ and writes its path here).
VISIT_CLIENT_PATH=
# The database's superuser (from 0.21), for setup only: `auth-client migrate --admin` makes visit-client's and
# auth-client's roles with it, and bin/setup brings them up to date. A secret. Never passed to any run: not to
# visit-client, auth-client, or the workroom's server.
VISIT_DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=

# -- A workroom's auth-client: its sign-in (auth/INTEGRATING.md) ------------------------------------------
# auth-client reads these from its environment (each is also a flag: AUTH_PORT is --port), and VISIT_PORT and
# VISIT_TOKEN_FILE above, for /v1/visit. The launcher passes them on; the workroom's server gets AUTH_PORT and
# AUTH_TOKEN_FILE.

# Its database: Visit's, as auth-client's own role (bin/setup makes it): postgres://auth:password@host:port/database.
# A secret.
AUTH_DATABASE_URL=
# Its port on 127.0.0.1 (default 7403).
AUTH_PORT=
# The file the launcher writes a new service token to on every run (mode 0600), for auth-client and the
# workroom's server. The token itself never goes in a .env.
AUTH_TOKEN_FILE=
# A session ends after this long unused, and this long in all: a number and s, m, h or d (default 7d and 30d).
AUTH_IDLE=
AUTH_MAX_AGE=
# Not auth-client's but its launcher's: where auth-client is (bin/setup puts it beside visit-client).
AUTH_CLIENT_PATH=

# -- Running the lobby (lobby/README.md, "Put it on a server") -------------------------------------------
# The server bin/deploy-lobby deploys to (user@host, e.g. ubuntu@203.0.113.5) and its ssh key file, if
# ssh needs one. It fills these in itself on the first deploy.
LOBBY_DEPLOY=
LOBBY_DEPLOY_KEY=
# The directory it deploys into on the server (default basedverse-lobby), for a server set up
# under another name.
LOBBY_DEPLOY_DIR=
# The address of the lobby it last deployed (it writes it; bin/setup offers it).
LOBBY_DEPLOY_URL=
